From 9d649c5774bef27bead774cd088ca8a6ba2fa885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:31:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: lever spring, lever friction, inert cone latch with a
 virtual latch and a door only probe fitted to the real robot records of 11-13
 (DoorSpawnerCfg.handle_spring_stiffness_range and handle_spring_preload_range
 make the lever return torque grow with angle as on the real lever, 0.27 N m
 at 0 deg and 1.42 N m per rad, instead of the constant drive max force; Isaac
 Lab writes the drive target 0 every step so the preload is the handle effort
 applied by the env, minus the preload instead of the 0.26 N m tension, and
 the lever body gravity is switched off because the real torque is net of it;
 the old damping of 0.5 per deg (29 N m s per rad) was hidden by the max force
 and is replaced by handle_spring_damping 0.3; handle_friction_range binds a
 physics material with max combine to the lever bars; latch_inert removes the
 cone collider and widens the latch joint limit because the cone was pushed in
 by the frame before any touch, turning the lever 13 to 26 deg, its joint
 limit stopped the lever at the release angle, and pushing the door cammed it
 open; env.config.virtual_latch holds the hinge with a stiff one sided spring
 while the lever is above the release angle and the door is within zone_deg of
 closed; env.config.lever_probe pushes each lever with a different torque and
 then the hinge, and on the fitted door the settled lever angles matched the
 set spring within 0.05 deg in 15 of 15 free envs and the door opened exactly
 in the 32 of 32 envs above the release angle; per env lever and latch values
 go to static.npz as door_lever_*; default off = unchanged) (11-14)

